  "body": "Support Haas extended work coordinate offsets `G154 P1` through `G154 P99` across setup definitions, probing, and `assets/posts/haas.cps`.\n\nToday, `crates/app/src/operation/types/sel.rs:6` restricts `WCS_SLOTS` to six values (`G54`–`G59`). Setup validation (`crates/app/src/setup.rs`), posting (`crates/app/src/posting.rs:1088`), project serialization, UI pickers, and MCP tools (`crates/app/src/mcp/setup_tools.rs`) all index that six-item list.\nInside `assets/posts/haas.cps` (`slotOf()` and `onProbeResult()`, lines `627-731`), the post only maps `G54`–`G59` to `#5221+` and `G10 L2 P1..P6`. Any other offset silently falls back to `G54`.\n\nImplement these changes:\n- Extend setup work-offset representation so setups can hold extended work offsets (`G154 P1`–`G154 P99`) alongside `G54`–`G59`. Document the schema design in `docs/decisions/`.\n- Refuse extended offsets cleanly by name when posting for controls or posts that do not support them. Never fall back silently to `G54`.\n- Update `assets/posts/haas.cps` to emit `G154 Pn` in `startPreamble()` and update `onProbeResult()` to emit `G10 L20 Pn` and `#14001 + 20 * (n - 1)` for `G154 P1`–`P99`.\n\nDone means: A setup can select `G154 P1`–`P99`, unsupported posts refuse it by name, and `haas.cps` tests verify `G154 Pn`, `G10 L20 Pn`, and `#14001+` probing output.\n\nPart of #1961\n",
